menu "Wi-Fi Toolbox"

    config TOOLBOX_ALLOW_INJECTION
        bool "Offer frame injection in the app"
        default y
        help
            With this off, InjectStart is refused on the host so the build cannot
            ask the co-processor to transmit. On its own that would be a false
            sense of safety — the injecting code lives in the co-processor's
            firmware — so a shipped image must also be built with the
            co-processor's WIFI_TOOLBOX_ALLOW_INJECTION off. That flag lives with
            the co-processor component (components/wifi_toolbox/Kconfig).

            Capture and the net utilities are unaffected.

endmenu

menu "BLE Toolbox"

    config BLE_TOOLBOX_ALLOW_SPAM
        bool "Compile the BLE Toolbox's advertisement transmit path"
        default y
        help
            Builds the BLE Spam screen and the code behind it. The gate is
            enforced in this firmware: an explicit acknowledgement, a duration
            capped and re-checked on every tick, non-connectable and
            non-scannable frames, and an indicator for as long as it transmits.

            Off removes the code rather than hiding the button.

endmenu

    config TOOLBOX_SCREENSHOT_SERVER
        bool "Serve the screen over HTTP for diagnostics"
        default n
        help
            Starts a small HTTP server on the board's Wi-Fi address that serves
            the current framebuffer as a BMP. A bench aid for a development
            build: it exposes the screen to anyone on the network with no
            authentication, so it is OFF by default.
